{"qid":"Q1013","names":["Lesotho"],"title":"Lesotho","endonym":{"native":"Lesotho","lang":"st"},"capsule":"The Kingdom of Lesotho is a constitutional monarchy entirely surrounded by South Africa, successor to the British Protectorate of Basutoland, which achieved independence on 4 October 1966 under King Moshoeshoe II. The country's political history has been turbulent: Prime Minister Leabua Jonathan suspended the constitution after losing the 1970 elections, military coups followed in 1986 and 1991, and instability has persisted through the 2010s. Lesotho's economy depends on textile exports, remittances from mineworkers in South Africa, and water royalties from the Lesotho Highlands Water Project, a major infrastructure scheme delivering water to South Africa.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Lesotho's borders are precisely defined and uncontested; its political and territorial status as an enclave state is thoroughly documented.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Lesotho","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lesotho"},{"label":"Britannica: Lesotho","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Lesotho"}],"britannica":"place/Lesotho","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Lesotho","rulers":[{"qid":"Q544951","name":"Moshoeshoe II of Lesotho","start":1970,"end":1990,"image":"Moshoeshoe II van Lesotho.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Moshoeshoe%20II%20van%20Lesotho.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 nl","artist":"Joost Evers / Anefo","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Moshoeshoe wa Bobedi wa Lesotho","nativeLang":"st"},{"qid":"Q57537","name":"Letsie III of Lesotho","start":1990,"end":1995,"image":"Letsie III.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Letsie%20III.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","artist":"IAEA Imagebank","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Letsie III","nativeLang":"st"},{"qid":"Q1567660","name":"Hae Phoofolo","start":1994,"end":1994,"image":null},{"qid":"Q459286","name":"Mamohato of Lesotho","start":1996,"end":1996,"image":null},{"qid":"Q57732","name":"Pakalitha Mosisili","start":1998,"end":2012,"image":"Pakalitha Mosisili with Obamas cropped.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Pakalitha%20Mosisili%20with%20Obamas%20cropped.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Pakalitha_Mosisili_with_Obamas.jpg: Official White House Photo by Lawrence Jackson\nderivative work: Entheta (talk)","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q983971","name":"Tom Thabane","start":2014,"end":2015,"image":"Tom Thabane cropped.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Tom%20Thabane%20cropped.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"OGL v1.0","artist":"Foreign and Commonwealth Office","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q91621859","name":"Moeketsi Majoro","start":2020,"end":2022,"image":"Moeketsi Majoro (01910409) (9654273280) (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Moeketsi%20Majoro%20(01910409)%20(9654273280)%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 2.0","artist":"IAEA Imagebank","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q114588964","name":"Sam Matekane","start":2022,"end":null,"image":"Sam Matekane candidate (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Sam%20Matekane%20candidate%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Attribution","artist":"European Union Election Observation Mission Lesotho 2022","attributionRequired":false}}],"edited":"w3"}